&lt;h1 id=&quot;neocloud-bd-pursuit-specialist-account-executive&quot; data-lfile-container=&quot;fe3c1b5e-3a17-4c7d-83ae-8c57fdfd4e57&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;NeoCloud BD Pursuit Specialist / Account Executive&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backblaze (Nasdaq: BLZE)&lt;/strong&gt; | Reports to the Head of NeoCloud Sales&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;how-we-got-here&quot;&gt;How We Got Here&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We started by building storage servers from scratch in a Palo Alto apartment to save 90% on hardware. Turns out hard constraints make for pretty good engineering. That discipline forged a platform that performs as well or better than competitors, scales to multi-exabyte workloads, and costs a fraction of what AWS or Google charge. AI infrastructure runs on data. Storage gets hard at scale. We&#39;ve been breaking, rebuilding, and improving that storage layer for 20 years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, the world&#39;s leading AI infrastructure providers, neoclouds, and data-intensive businesses run on Backblaze. Our platform includes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;B2 Overdrive&lt;/strong&gt; - high-throughput object storage engineered for AI infrastructure, GPU workloads, and massive-scale data pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;B2 Neo&lt;/strong&gt; - white-label enterprise cloud storage powering neocloud platforms for AI, HPC, and media&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;B2 Cloud Storage&lt;/strong&gt; - S3-compatible object storage with predictable pricing, free egress, and no lock-in&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Computer Backup&lt;/strong&gt; - automatic, continuous endpoint backup for Macs and PCs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;500,000+ customers. 175 countries. Nasdaq: BLZE. backblaze.com&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;the-role&quot;&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NeoClouds are GPU-rich, AI-native infrastructure providers, and they need fast, affordable, S3-compatible storage at scale. Backblaze is the high-performance capacity storage layer for AI. You will win these accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a new-logo role. You will own a named set of NeoClouds from the top 80 worldwide and pursue them from first meeting to signed contract.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not an inbound role. If you want a defined territory and a queue of warm leads, it isn&#39;t the right fit. If your instinct is to pick an account, find the engineer who feels the storage cost first, and work up to the CXO, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-you-will-do&quot;&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pursue named accounts.&lt;/strong&gt; Build a pursuit plan for each account. Map the buying group from infrastructure engineers to the CXO, and build relationships across it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run discovery.&lt;/strong&gt; Learn how each NeoCloud runs its stack, where storage costs and performance limit it, and how Backblaze fits. Work with the Sales Engineer and Field CTO on technical validation and proof-of-concept testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Choose the route.&lt;/strong&gt; Your motion is Sell-To. Decide with your manager when an account also calls for Sell-With, which Strategic Partnerships runs with the Head of NeoCloud Sales. When a partner such as NVIDIA, Super Micro, Weka, VAST, or AMD helps win the account, bring in Strategic Partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the deal.&lt;/strong&gt; Work with your manager and legal on multi-year commitments, SLAs, and revenue share when Backblaze runs behind a NeoCloud&#39;s storage service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sell inside Backblaze.&lt;/strong&gt; Pull Cloud Operations and Engineering into the integration early. Their time is as scarce as your buyer&#39;s, and you will earn it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Line up executive sponsors.&lt;/strong&gt; Secure a Backblaze executive sponsor and a customer executive sponsor on every priority account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hand off and expand.&lt;/strong&gt; Bring in the strategic account manager in Customer Success as customers go live, and stay in the account as it grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep the forecast honest.&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain accurate pipeline, next steps, and close dates in the CRM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-we-are-looking-for&quot;&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure sales expertise&lt;/strong&gt;, with a record of closing complex, multi-year deals in storage, cloud, compute, networking, or data center infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical fluency.&lt;/strong&gt; You run most technical conversations with infrastructure engineers and architects about GPU clusters, networking, and storage yourself, and earn their trust. The Sales Engineer owns deeper validation and proofs of concept&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive presence.&lt;/strong&gt; You have built VP, SVP, and CTO relationships and can lead those meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hunter drive.&lt;/strong&gt; You open doors in accounts that do not know you yet, and you stay with a long pursuit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seller of record.&lt;/strong&gt; You have carried a quota and closed deals with your name on them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal structure experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You have negotiated SLA, IP, and revenue-share terms on deals you closed, not just understood them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team play.&lt;/strong&gt; You work well with sales engineers, partner teams, and operations teams to land one account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;also-true-of-the-right-person&quot;&gt;Also True of the Right Person&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships with NeoCloud technical or executive leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with OEM, ISV, or co-sell motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with S3-compatible object storage, data egress economics, and AI/ML data pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;this-is-not-the-role-for-you-if&quot;&gt;This Is Not the Role for You If&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want a defined territory or an inbound queue rather than named accounts you have to open&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You prefer a short sales cycle to a long pursuit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You hand technical questions to someone else and wait for the answer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want to bring a SaaS motion here unchanged&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work accounts alone rather than with sales engineering, partners, and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;how-we-will-interview&quot;&gt;How We Will Interview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will ask you to walk us through a pursuit you ran from first meeting to signed contract, including a long one that stalled and how you kept it moving. We will ask how you earned an infrastructure engineer&#39;s trust. We will ask for your own view of how you would approach this role. You will hold cross-functional conversations with the Sales Engineer and the Field CTO, because you will pursue accounts with them. And you will go through a panel, so we can see how you work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Backblaze, we value being fair and good to our customers, partners, and employees. Diversity, equity, and inclusion are at the core of our values. We are committed to fostering a workforce where all employees feel a sense of belonging regardless of race, ethnicity, nationality, gender, sexual orientation, age, religion, socio-economic status, ability, veteran status, and education. We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Backblaze is the object storage leader in the open cloud movement, fueling customer success with cloud storage built purposefully to unlock budgets, unburden administrators, and unleash innovators. Together with our partners, we’re helping customers break free from the restrictive, overpriced legacy solutions that hold them back, and blaze forward with the full power of the open cloud in their hands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2007, we scaled the business with less than $3 million in outside funding until 2021, when we did a traditional IPO on the Nasdaq stock exchange. Today, Backblaze generates over $100m in revenue and is the leading specialized storage cloud - managing over three billion gigabytes of data storage for 500K+ customers in 175+ countries, including businesses, developers, IT professionals, and individuals. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;But while there is a lot to celebrate in our past, there is almost as much opportunity ahead of us. We are seeking an &lt;strong&gt;AI Workflow Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backblaze is running a company-wide AI transformation program, and this role is where strategy becomes something you can actually use. As AI Workflow Engineer, you will be the hands-on builder inside the AI Program Office - embedded alongside the Director, AI Enablement, and deployed into non-GTM, non-Engineering business teams to prototype, build, and ship AI-powered workflow solutions that make a measurable difference in how work gets done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a research role or a strategy role. You will spend your time building: prompt architectures, automation flows, lightweight agents, API integrations, and demos that help a business team see - concretely - what AI can do for them. You will move across functions, which means you need to understand how businesses actually operate. The ideal background is someone who started in a business-facing role - finance, operations, marketing, customer success, HR - and developed serious hands-on AI and automation skills on top of that foundation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with the Director, AI Enablement, who owns the program management and delivery layer. Your job is to make their scoped solutions real - fast, iteratively, and with enough rigor that what you build can go to production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and Ship AI Workflow Solutions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take scoped use cases from the Director, AI Enablement and build working solutions: prompt layers, automation flows, lightweight agents, RAG implementations, and API integrations that connect AI tools to the systems business teams already use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build working prototypes quickly - the goal is to show a team what is possible in days, not weeks, then refine based on what actually lands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate a documented workflow assessment into a technical design, select the right tools for the job, and own the build through to a deployable solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain solution documentation that is clear enough for handoff, iteration, and audit - not just for engineers, but for the business owner who will live with it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Embed in Business Teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spend time inside the functions you are building for - Finance, HR, Legal, Marketing Ops, Customer Success, and others - understanding how the work actually flows before you redesign it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run working sessions with team members to map current-state workflows, surface friction points, and identify where AI creates real leverage versus where it creates noise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build credibility with non-technical stakeholders by showing them working solutions, not decks - and by being honest about what will and will not work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support user acceptance testing and early adoption, troubleshooting issues close to launch and iterating based on real usage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support the AI Program Office&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build demos and proof-of-concepts that help the Director, AI Enablement make the case for a use case - or disqualify it early before resources are committed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to vendor and tool evaluations with a builder&#39;s perspective: not just whether a tool claims to do something, but whether it actually works in the context of a specific workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed learnings from the build process back into the program - what worked, what did not, what should be standardized across functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on tactical quick wins and longer-horizon strategic builds at the same time, switching contexts across active use cases as priorities shift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like (First 90 Days)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have completed at least one workflow assessment alongside the Director and produced a working prototype from it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least one solution you built is in active use by a business team, with a named owner and feedback loop in place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have worked inside at least two different business functions and understand their core workflows well enough to identify the next use case without being told&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Director, AI Enablement trusts you to own the build layer independently - scoping conversations happen together, execution happens with you driving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Right Fit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-4 years of experience that includes meaningful time working inside a business-facing function - operations, finance, marketing, customer success, HR, or similar - not just in Engineering or IT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building with AI tools: prompt engineering, automation platforms (Make, Zapier, n8n, or equivalent), API integrations, and at least working familiarity with RAG architectures and agent frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to take a messy real-world process, understand it from the inside, and build something that makes it faster or better - not just technically cleaner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with non-technical stakeholders: you can explain what you are building without jargon, gather requirements without a formal spec, and manage expectations when a prototype needs three more iterations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong enough with code or no-code tools to get solutions to a deployable state independently - you do not need an engineer to ship your work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to manage multiple active projects at different stages without dropping anything - a quick win in HR this week does not mean the Finance automation waits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuinely curious about how companies work: the org chart, the incentives, the handoffs, the bottlenecks. This is what separates a good AI builder from a great one in a business context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience working in or closely with G&amp;amp;A, Finance, Legal, Marketing Ops, or Customer Success teams - you have lived in the workflows you will be redesigning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI governance basics: data handling, PII awareness, and when a use case needs a security or privacy review before it ships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a small program or startup environment where you wore multiple hats and shipped without a lot of process overhead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in cloud infrastructure, SaaS, or storage companies - comfort with technical products and the teams that build them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio, GitHub, or examples of AI workflows or automations you have built - something you can show, not just describe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Backblaze, we value being fair and good to our customers, partners, and employees. That’s why diversity, equity, and inclusion are at the core of our values. We are committed to fostering a workforce where all employees feel a sense of belonging regardless of race, ethnicity, nationality, gender, sexual orientation, age, religion, socio-economic status, ability, veteran status, and education. We believe that our dedication to cultivating a diverse workspace not only allows us to better serve our customers in over 175 countries, but further reinforces our commitment to doing the right thing.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To understand more about the data we collect and process as part of your application, please view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63d32de856f6323a43a277f2/64b0660cd90ac9b4953f7f1d_Backblaze_HR_Employee_Related_Privacy_Notice.pdf&quot;&gt;Backblaze Employee Privacy Notice.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;#LATAM&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Backblaze&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backblaze is the object storage leader in the open cloud movement, fueling customer success with cloud storage built purposefully to unlock budgets, unburden administrators, and unleash innovators. Together with our partners, we’re helping customers break free from the restrictive, overpriced legacy solutions that hold them back, and blaze forward with the full power of the open cloud in their hands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2007, we scaled the business with less than $3 million in outside funding until 2021, when we did a traditional IPO on the Nasdaq stock exchange. Today, Backblaze generates over $100m in revenue and is the leading specialized storage cloud - managing over three billion gigabytes of data storage for 500K+ customers in 175+ countries, including businesses, developers, IT professionals, and individuals.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;But while there is a lot to celebrate in our past, there is almost as much opportunity ahead of us. Backblaze is seeking a highly analytical,&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;systems-oriented &lt;strong&gt;Cluster &amp;amp; Systems Capacity Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to drive the planning, forecasting, deployment, and optimization of hardware infrastructure across our global cloud storage platform.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role ensures that Backblaze’s storage clusters, compute systems, and network infrastructure scale reliably, cost-efficiently, and ahead of demand. You will build and maintain predictive models, ensure consistent supply and demand alignment, and partner cross-functionally to inform strategic investment and deployment decisions. .&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact role within Cloud Operations, directly contributing to service availability, durability, performance, margin optimization, and long-term platform scalability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Capacity Planning &amp;amp; Forecasting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain short, medium, and long-term capacity demand and hardware deployment forecasts across storage, compute, and network domains within the platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build predictive models that translate business demand signals into infrastructure requirements using historical utilization, growth trends, product sales plans, hardware lifecycle roadmaps, and other key business inputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Infrastructure, Production, and Network Engineering teams to align capacity plans with system design and scaling initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and automate forecasting pipelines, simulation calculators and tools, and capacity dashboards to improve data quality, reduce manual analysis, and provide stakeholders clear visibility into platform usage and cluster health metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cluster Performance &amp;amp; Resource Optimization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyze cluster and system-level utilization and performance across CPU, memory, IOPS, and network resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adjust deployment plans and recommended configurations in real-time to maintain adequate headroom and system stability in support of delivering a world-class customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with service and platform owners to develop headroom and live buffer policies, optimize hardware BoMs, leverage virtualized orchestration, and reduce product cost&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional Organizational Alignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in lockstep with Operations and Finance peers to align capacity plans and hardware requirements with capital budgets, cost targets, and financial outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support strategic optimization initiatives across infrastructure investments, engineering development, and operations processes, contributing to long-term infrastructure strategy and capital planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead efforts to evaluate, procure, and provision requests for new or additional hardware, working with Systems and Network Engineering, SRE, NOC, and Data Center Operations teams to identify and deliver optimal solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain alignment with Product and Sales to support customer onboarding, growth, and demand variability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate complex capacity and infrastructure insights clearly to technical and non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, Data Science, Information Systems, Statistics or a related, technical field (or equivalent experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-6+ years of experience in Site Reliability Engineering, Infrastructure Capacity Planning, Systems/Infrastructure Engineering, Production Engineering, Data Center Operations or similar Cloud Operations role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity and experience working with Cloud Storage infrastructure, particularly highly-available, large-scale distributed systems supporting large amounts of data with high throughput and complex performance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in capacity modeling, performance analysis, scenario modeling, and/or infrastructure cost optimization, with an ability to quantify ideas within financial frameworks and forecasts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in database and data analysis tools (preferably Snowflake, Metabase, Grafana, Python, SQL, Prometheus, Victoria Metrics, and Excel/Google Sheets)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated deep, creative, and logical thinking complimented by a strong data analysis skillset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and documentation skills, with the ability to share knowledge and explain concepts accurately and concisely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire to work on a highly-autonomous team that cares deeply about quality, cost, and the customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backblaze Perks:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare for family, including dental and vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation and 401K&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RSU grants for full-time employees&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ESPP program&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible vacation policy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MacBook Pro to use for work, plus a generous stipend to personalize your&amp;nbsp; workstation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Childcare bonus (human children only)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fertility treatment and support&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning &amp;amp; development program&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture that supports a healthy work-life balance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;At this point, we hope you&#39;re feeling excited about the job description you&#39;re reading. Even if you don&#39;t meet every requirement, we still encourage you to apply. Learning, developing, and growing are key parts of our culture. We&#39;re eager to meet people who believe in our mission and can contribute to our team in various ways. We want people to feel comfortable expressing their true selves and to come, stay, and do their best work here.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;To provide greater transparency to candidates, we share base pay ranges for all US-based job postings regardless of state. We set standard base pay ranges for all roles based on function, level, and country location, benchmarked against similar-stage growth companies. Final offer amounts are determined by multiple factors, including candidate location, skills, depth of work experience, and relevant licenses/credentials, and may vary from the amounts listed below.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected salary range for this role is $123,000 - $175,000.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Backblaze, we value being fair and good to our customers, partners, and employees. That’s why diversity, equity, and inclusion are at the core of our values. We are committed to fostering a workforce where all employees feel a sense of belonging regardless of race, ethnicity, nationality, gender, sexual orientation, age, religion, socio-economic status, ability, veteran status, and education. We believe that our dedication to cultivating a diverse workspace not only allows us to better serve our customers in over 175 countries but further reinforces our commitment to doing the right thing. We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To understand more about the data we collect and process as part of your application, please view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63d32de856f6323a43a277f2/64b0660cd90ac9b4953f7f1d_Backblaze_HR_Employee_Related_Privacy_Notice.pdf&quot;&gt;Backblaze Employee Privacy Notice.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Backblaze&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backblaze is the object storage leader in the open cloud movement, fueling customer success with cloud storage built purposefully to unlock budgets, unburden administrators, and unleash innovators. Together with our partners, we’re helping customers break free from the restrictive, overpriced legacy solutions that hold them back, and blaze forward with the full power of the open cloud in their hands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2007, we scaled the business with less than $3 million in outside funding until 2021, when we did a traditional IPO on the Nasdaq stock exchange. Today, Backblaze generates over $100m in revenue and is the leading specialized storage cloud - managing over three billion gigabytes of data storage for 500K+ customers in 175+ countries, including businesses, developers, IT professionals, and individuals.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;But while there is a lot to celebrate in our past, there is almost as much opportunity ahead of us. We’re seeking a&lt;strong&gt; Data Center Technician &lt;/strong&gt;to join our team!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Individuals fulfilling this role will be responsible for managing, maintaining, and optimizing the physical infrastructure of our data center operations. The ideal candidate will have significant technical knowledge of server hardware, networking equipment, power and cooling systems, and structured cabling. This role requires a proactive problem-solver with strong leadership abilities, deductive reasoning, and a focus on operational excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hardware Deployment &amp;amp; Maintenance:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain organizational infrastructure including racking equipment, replacing hard drives and other system components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot, repair, and replace defective equipment with minimal supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help manage onsite inventory of hard drives, cables, rails and other spare parts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RMA defective components&lt;/li&gt;
