&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Backblaze&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backblaze is the object storage leader in the open cloud movement, fueling customer success with cloud storage built purposefully to unlock budgets, unburden administrators, and unleash innovators. Together with our partners, we’re helping customers break free from the restrictive, overpriced legacy solutions that hold them back, and blaze forward with the full power of the open cloud in their hands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2007, we scaled the business with less than $3 million in outside funding until 2021, when we did a traditional IPO on the Nasdaq stock exchange. Today, Backblaze generates over $100m in revenue and is the leading specialized storage cloud - managing over three billion gigabytes of data storage for 500K+ customers in 175+ countries, including businesses, developers, IT professionals, and individuals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Want to know what you’ll be doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work on our data infrastructure platform which supports the B2 Object Storage and Computer Backup products, responsible for the data infrastructure that everything runs on. You will help improve automation, observability and stability for durability, increase throughput, and drive architectural changes to support the long term requirements of our service.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build automation frameworks that let other engineers provision, configure, and repair fleet infrastructure themselves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and extend the observability stack (metrics, logs, traces, alerts) that tells us whether the storage platform is healthy and where it is degrading&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reporting, dashboards, and visualizations that give engineering and leadership a clear view into fleet health, capacity, and operational trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build system health tooling that detects failing hardware, drifting configuration, and capacity risk before they turn into incidents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical design discussions and produce clear design documents for changes that span multiple services and teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the implementation of large features from design through rollout, including the migration and backfill work that real systems require&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the on-call rotation to turn recurring toil and incident findings into automation and better signal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Right Fit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of backend development in an enterprise environment, working in an object-oriented or systems language (Java, Rust, C++, C#, Go, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing automation frameworks or platforms that other engineers build on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building large scale software systems running on thousands of servers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building automation or tooling that other engineers depend on daily, whether internal platform services, operational tooling, or a deployment and configuration pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of an observability stack (Prometheus, Grafana, OpenTelemetry, ELK, Datadog, or equivalent), including instrumenting a service and designing alerts people trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Linux fundamentals and comfort operating in a bare-metal or hybrid environment rather than a fully managed cloud&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional experience incorporating AI-assisted development tools (Gemini, Cursor, Claude Code, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with all aspects of the software development lifecycle, including design, implementation, testing, and rollout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exhibits curiosity and seeks to understand before offering solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicates proactively in a remote environment by keeping the team informed, surfacing blockers early, and moving work forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applies analytical thinking to ambiguous problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Java&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with configuration management or infrastructure-as-code tooling (Ansible, Salt, Puppet, Chef, Terraform)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing SLOs and error budgets, or reducing alert noise on a fleet running at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with time-series databases and query languages such as PromQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience automating hardware lifecycle work: burn-in, failure detection, drive replacement, decommissioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with discovering and implementing performance improvements, including CPU and IO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of Linux internals and file systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with hard drive performance and optimization, including host-managed SMR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and interpreting models, dashboards, or reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required for all Backblaze Employees:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good attitude and willingness to do whatever it takes to get the job done&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong desire to work for a small, fast-paced company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire to learn and adapt to rapidly changing technologies and work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigorous adherence to best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relentless attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent interpersonal skills and good oral/written communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent troubleshooting and problem solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backblaze Perks:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare for family, including dental and vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation and 401K&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RSU grants for full-time employees&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ESPP program&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible vacation policy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MacBook Pro to use for work plus a generous stipend to personalize your&amp;nbsp; workstation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Childcare bonus (human children only)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fertility treatment and support&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning &amp;amp; development program&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture that supports a healthy work-life balance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To provide greater transparency to candidates, we share base pay ranges for all US-based job postings regardless of state. We set standard base pay ranges for all roles based on function, level, and country location, benchmarked against similar-stage growth companies. Final offer amounts are determined by multiple factors, including candidate location, skills, depth of work experience, and relevant licenses/credentials, and may vary from the amounts listed below.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base pay range for this position is:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$175,000 - $200,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Backblaze, we value being fair and good to our customers, partners, and employees. That’s why diversity, equity, and inclusion are at the core of our values. We are committed to fostering a workforce where all employees feel a sense of belonging regardless of race, ethnicity, nationality, gender, sexual orientation, age, religion, socio-economic status, ability, veteran status, and education. We believe that our dedication to cultivating a diverse workspace not only allows us to better serve our customers in over 175 countries, but further reinforces our commitment to doing the right thing. &lt;strong&gt;We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To understand more about the data we collect and process as part of your application, please view our &lt;a href=&quot;https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63d32de856f6323a43a277f2/64b0660cd90ac9b4953f7f1d_Backblaze_HR_Employee_Related_Privacy_Notice.pdf&quot;&gt;Backblaze Employee Privacy Notice.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Backblaze&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backblaze is the object storage leader in the open cloud movement, fueling customer success with cloud storage built purposefully to unlock budgets, unburden administrators, and unleash innovators. Together with our partners, we&#39;re helping customers break free from the restrictive, overpriced legacy solutions that hold them back, and blaze forward with the full power of the open cloud in their hands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2007, we scaled the business with less than $3 million in outside funding until 2021, when we did a traditional IPO on the Nasdaq stock exchange. Today, Backblaze generates over $100m in revenue and is the leading specialized storage cloud—managing over three billion gigabytes of data storage for 500K+ customers in 175+ countries, including businesses, developers, IT professionals, and individuals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First Line of Defense:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the primary point of contact for customer-affecting technical issues and lead real-time incident resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Adhere to incident management protocols and drive post-mortems to capture process improvements and root-cause analyses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monitoring &amp;amp; Alerting:&lt;/strong&gt; Monitor and respond to Zabbix, Grafana and Opensearch alerts—taking direct remediation steps or managing seamless escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure &amp;amp; Pod Health:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure the health and reliability of storage pods across all sites (defining and refining monitoring alert definitions and completing daily tasks relating to hardware replacement diagnosis, system troubleshooting and executing needed configuration changes via Ansible and a Git repository framework).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Center Tech Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as an escalation point for Data Center Technicians regarding advanced pod troubleshooting, deployment queries, migration issues, and Ansible playbooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrations &amp;amp; Provisioning:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage pre-deployment configuration and testing for Vault systems, initiate Vault migrations, and perform health checks on migration pods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code Deployments: Use Jenkins to deploy code updates across all our environments.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Network &amp;amp; Operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify and escalate network anomalies, document network IP assignments for upcoming deployments, and track server farm releases/updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation &amp;amp; Process:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify opportunities to automate daily operational tasks and document workflow procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-Call &amp;amp; Flexibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in an on-call rotation shift, with flexibility to work outside standard business hours (including weekends, evenings, or holidays) as operational needs arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Right Fit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 2–4 years of hands-on experience in Systems Administration, Linux Operations, or SRE environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Fundamentals:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong foundational understanding of Linux systems, command-line interfaces, network cabling/topologies, and IP network classifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem Solving &amp;amp; Automation:&lt;/strong&gt; Analytical mindset with a drive to learn, troubleshoot complex hardware/software interactions, and automate repetitive tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent cross-functional communication and collaboration skills with both technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity, &amp;amp; Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Even if you don’t meet 100% of the qualifications listed above, we still encourage you to apply! Learning, developing, and growing are key parts of our culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Backblaze, diversity, equity, and inclusion are core to our values. We are committed to fostering a workplace where all employees feel a sense of belonging regardless of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, or veteran status.&lt;/p&gt;
