&lt;p&gt;Backblaze is the object storage leader in the open cloud movement, fueling customer success with cloud storage built purposefully to unlock budgets, unburden administrators, and unleash innovators. Together with our partners, we’re helping customers break free from the restrictive, overpriced legacy solutions that hold them back, and blaze forward with the full power of the open cloud in their hands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2007, we scaled the business with less than $3 million in outside funding until 2021, when we did a traditional IPO on the Nasdaq stock exchange. Today, Backblaze generates over $100m in revenue and is the leading specialized storage cloud - managing over three billion gigabytes of data storage for 500K+ customers in 175+ countries, including businesses, developers, IT professionals, and individuals.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;But while there is a lot to celebrate in our past, there is almost as much opportunity ahead of us. We are seeking a&lt;strong&gt; Sr. AI Security Engineer &lt;/strong&gt;to join our team!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backblaze is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Senior AI Security Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to design and implement safeguards for &lt;strong&gt;internal AI usage&lt;/strong&gt;, with a focus on &lt;strong&gt;agentic systems, developer protection, and runtime security&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role for a practitioner who has &lt;strong&gt;built and deployed security controls&lt;/strong&gt;, not just defined policy. You will enable teams to safely use AI by creating &lt;strong&gt;enforcement layers, identity controls, and detection capabilities&lt;/strong&gt; that constrain and monitor AI-driven activity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agentic AI Safeguards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and implement &lt;strong&gt;guardrails for tool-using AI systems&lt;/strong&gt;, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tool access controls and allowlists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Context and memory isolation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Step-level validation of agent actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply mitigations aligned to the &lt;strong&gt;OWASP Agentic AI Top 10&lt;/strong&gt; (e.g., prompt injection, unsafe tool use, data leakage, excessive autonomy)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Runtime Security Controls&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build &lt;strong&gt;enforcement mechanisms&lt;/strong&gt; that govern AI behavior at execution time:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interceptors, proxies, or middleware for tool/API calls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Policy decision and enforcement layers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rate limits, execution bounds, and kill-switches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prevent unsafe or unauthorized actions initiated by AI systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Non-Human Identity (NHI)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement &lt;strong&gt;identity and access controls for agents and automation&lt;/strong&gt;, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short-lived credentials and scoped permissions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear separation between human and non-human access&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong binding of identity to task context and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all AI actions are &lt;strong&gt;attributable and auditable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Observability &amp;amp; Detection&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement &lt;strong&gt;logging and tracing for AI activity&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prompts, tool usage, and decision flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build detection capabilities using:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Behavioral baselining and anomaly detection techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and alert on:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Abnormal tool usage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Suspicious prompt patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unexpected data access&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Threat Modeling (MAESTRO)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform &lt;strong&gt;agentic system threat modeling using MAESTRO&lt;/strong&gt;, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mapping agent capabilities, trust boundaries, and attack paths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modeling misuse and adversarial scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate findings into &lt;strong&gt;practical safeguards and detection logic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developer Safeguards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protect developers using AI tools by:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preventing sensitive data exposure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validating AI-generated code and actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Constraining unsafe automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable safe usage of AI-assisted development tools (e.g., &lt;strong&gt;Claude Code, Codex, Cursor&lt;/strong&gt;) with:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security validation layers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Controlled prompting and output handling patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Right Fit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in &lt;strong&gt;security engineering or backend systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience &lt;strong&gt;designing and deploying security controls&lt;/strong&gt;, such as:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Runtime enforcement layers (proxies, middleware, policy engines)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identity and access systems, especially for non-human entities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills (Python preferred; Go, Java, or TypeScript a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using &lt;strong&gt;AI-assisted development tools such as Claude Code&lt;/strong&gt; in real workflows, including understanding associated security risks and safeguards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Logging, monitoring, and detection systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building or securing API/service interactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical familiarity with:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agentic AI systems or tool-integrated LLM workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OWASP guidance for AI/agent risks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Practitioner Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying (not just referencing):&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OWASP Agentic AI / LLM risk guidance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NIST AI RMF&lt;/strong&gt; concepts in real systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CSA guidance&lt;/strong&gt; on workload and machine identity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Zero Trust for non-human identities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secrets management and credential scoping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observability tooling (e.g., OpenTelemetry, ELK)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience securing &lt;strong&gt;internal AI platforms or developer-facing AI tools&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in &lt;strong&gt;detection engineering, threat hunting, or adversarial testing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with agent frameworks (e.g., LangChain, LlamaIndex)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring engineers and guiding secure design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At this point, we hope you&#39;re feeling excited about the job description you&#39;re reading. Even if you don&#39;t meet every requirement, we still encourage you to apply. Learning, developing, and growing are key parts of our culture. We&#39;re eager to meet people who believe in our mission and can contribute to our team in various ways. We want people to feel comfortable expressing their true selves and to come, stay, and do their best work here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Backblaze, we value being fair and good to our customers, partners, and employees. That’s why diversity, equity, and inclusion are at the core of our values. We are committed to fostering a workforce where all employees feel a sense of belonging regardless of race, ethnicity, nationality, gender, sexual orientation, age, religion, socio-economic status, ability, veteran status, and education. We believe that our dedication to cultivating a diverse workspace not only allows us to better serve our customers in over 175 countries, but further reinforces our commitment to doing the right thing. &lt;strong&gt;We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To understand more about the data we collect and process as part of your application, please view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63d32de856f6323a43a277f2/64b0660cd90ac9b4953f7f1d_Backblaze_HR_Employee_Related_Privacy_Notice.pdf&quot;&gt;Backblaze Employee Privacy Notice.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LATAM&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;Sr. Developer Relations Manager&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backblaze — Remote, US&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Compensation: $172,000–$215,000 base + equity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Backblaze&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backblaze is the object storage layer for AI and data-intensive workloads, fueling customer success with cloud storage purpose-built for scalable performance and economics. We make customers unstoppable by solving their toughest storage challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today we manage nearly 6 billion gigabytes of data for 500K+ customers across 175+ countries with fast growth among Neoclouds, GenAI companies, and companies reliant on data–heavy workloads. Developers are at the center of our next chapter, and we&#39;re serious about earning their trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Developer relations is evolving quickly. Coding agents, informed by reference architectures and machine-readable documentation, are increasingly making integration decisions on behalf of developers. And trust, transparency, and human interaction are more important than ever as open source ideals and corporate agendas are weirdly attacked, limited, or promoted by unexpected sources and trends.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backblaze B2 Cloud storage was launched as a result of developer demand and has been committed to the developer ecosystem since day one. Today, we are seeking a leader who can help us become more present and trusted than ever before in this space, both as the storage default for agent-led projects and as a leading source of support, inspiration, and enablement for developers who need storage for whatever they’re building.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Sr. Developer Relations Manager, you&#39;ll work across a strong set of existing assets — a mature docs team, an engineering team focused on AI ecosystem integrations, our Flamethrower Startup Program, a content org, and an outward-facing SE team — and coordinate their outputs into a coherent, credible developer presence that earns mindshare where it matters most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a program-defining role for someone who thinks in systems, works backwards from adoption goals, knows how to make a company technically credible with developers who haven&#39;t heard of it yet, and is comfortable both channeling and being the face of developer relationships at Backblaze.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Own&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developer Presence in the Agentic Stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The primary goal of this role is to ensure Backblaze B2 is the best storage layer for developers and for their agents. That means understanding how AI coders discover and evaluate infrastructure tools today: through MCP servers, coding agent contexts, reference architectures, SDKs, and machine-readable documentation. You&#39;ll work with the internal AI team to define what &quot;agent-ready&quot; means for Backblaze and drive execution against it across engineering, docs, and content.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Coordination&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role starts as an individual contributor, but you&#39;ll have real influence over a strong set of resources: an engineering team building integrations into AI tooling (MLFlow, ComfyUI, Hugging Face, popular agent frameworks), a docs team that can be directed toward structured, agent-consumable formats, a content org that can amplify what you build, and an SE team that can extend your enablement work, among a number of others at the company. Your job is to coordinate these teams around a unified developer strategy, keep that strategy moving, and share its outputs with the broader world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community and Ecosystem&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Developers trust other developers. You&#39;ll underscore Backblaze&#39;s credibility in the communities where AI builders live: GitHub, Discord, open source projects, developer events, and the growing ecosystem of AI infrastructure tooling. You&#39;ll elevate internal technical voices, use their expertise to build your own thought leadership in the space, and partner with ecosystem players, and show up in a way that is earned, not marketed. Critically, you should have a presence in this community before coming to the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developer Feedback Loop&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll maintain a tight feedback loop from the developer community back to product and engineering — surfacing adoption friction, unmet integration needs, and emerging patterns worth prioritizing. The Flamethrower Startup Program gives you direct access to early-stage builders who can serve as signal-rich canaries for what&#39;s working and what isn&#39;t.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Metrics and Program Accountability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll define what success looks like — developer signups, activation rates, B2 adoption in AI frameworks, community engagement, content reach — and own progress against it. We&#39;re building this program to drive real revenue, and you&#39;ll be expected to connect the dots between awareness and conversion. Success in this role opens the door to bringing on, or from elsewhere in the company, developer resources to grow the program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful DevRel, developer marketing, or developer experience leadership at a cloud infrastructure, open source, or AI tooling company. You&#39;ve built or significantly grown a developer program, not just contributed to one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand how agentic workflows are reshaping how developers discover and integrate infrastructure tools — and you have opinions about what that means for DevRel strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technically credible. You can read a codebase, evaluate an SDK, write a working integration, and have a real conversation with an engineer about tradeoffs. You don&#39;t need to be a full-time SWE, but you need to have been one, or close to it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worked, or started, without a large team. You know how to amplify yourself through cross-functional relationships, external partners, and community rather than headcount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator — to developers externally and to leadership internally. You can write a crisp technical tutorial and a clear exec summary with equal ease.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing presence in developer communities. A following, conference talks, open source contributions, a technical blog — some signal that developers pay attention when you show up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong plus:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with model training, data processing or generative media&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with how coding agents (Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, etc.) surface and recommend infrastructure tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with or building on top of open source frameworks in the AI/ML ecosystem (MLflow, DVC, Ray Data, WebDataset, and MosaicML Streaming)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience running or contributing to a startup/developer program (accelerator, cohort model, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Have to Work With&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You won&#39;t be starting from scratch. You&#39;ll work closely with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A mature, capable &lt;strong&gt;docs team&lt;/strong&gt; that can be directed toward agent-consumable documentation formats and structured reference content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong &lt;strong&gt;engineering team&lt;/strong&gt; dedicated to integrating Backblaze into the AI tooling ecosystem — building connectors, working on external integrations, and driving internal product improvements for developer use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flamethrower&lt;/strong&gt;, our startup program, which is already generating community energy and early-adopter signal among AI builders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An outward-facing &lt;strong&gt;solutions engineering team&lt;/strong&gt; that can extend your enablement work with hands-on technical support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;content org&lt;/strong&gt; that can help produce and amplify developer-facing assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active strategic work from &lt;strong&gt;Rawkode Academy&lt;/strong&gt; laying the DevRel foundation: audit, persona validation, content models, and engagement strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why This Matters Now&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Developers are making storage decisions earlier in the stack than ever before — often before they&#39;ve spoken to a salesperson, often through a coding agent recommending a reference architecture. Backblaze has the right product, the right price point, and a growing engineering investment behind this motion. What we need is the person who can translate that into developer conviction at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The window to establish Backblaze as the default AI storage layer is open now. This role exists to make sure we don&#39;t miss it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Backblaze Perks&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare for family, including dental and vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation and 401K&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RSU grants for full-time employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ESPP program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible vacation policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MacBook Pro plus a generous workstation stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Childcare bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fertility treatment and support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning &amp;amp; development program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture that supports a healthy work-life balance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To provide greater transparency to candidates, we share base pay ranges for all US-based job postings regardless of state. Final offer amounts are determined by multiple factors including candidate location, skills, depth of work experience, and relevant licenses/credentials.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected salary range for this role is $172,000 - $215,000 plus 20% target annual bonus and RSUs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Backblaze, we value being fair and good to our customers, partners, and employees. Diversity, equity, and inclusion are at the core of our values. We are committed to fostering a workforce where all employees feel a sense of belonging regardless of race, ethnicity, nationality, gender, sexual orientation, age, religion, socio-economic status, ability, veteran status, and education. We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Backblaze is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to fostering a workforce where all employees feel a sense of belonging regardless of race, ethnicity, nationality, gender, sexual orientation, age, religion, socio-economic status, ability, veteran status, and education.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Backblaze&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backblaze provides reliable, high-availability cloud storage and backup trusted by consumers, SMBs, enterprises, and developers in over 150 countries. Backblaze Computer Backup protects the data of hundreds of thousands of customers, backing up laptops and desktops across Windows and macOS to the Backblaze cloud. We build durable, scalable systems with a strong emphasis on reliability, product quality, and a great customer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Software Development Manager to lead the team responsible for Backblaze Computer Backup, spanning both the cross-platform desktop client and the backend services that receive, store, and restore customer data. The entire Computer Backup engineering team reports into this role, which you will run through Desktop and Backend Leads who own the day-to-day of their areas. You will set the long-term technical direction for the product, own its multi-quarter delivery strategy, and hold accountability for the team’s budget and results.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on management role. You will take part in architecture discussions, code reviews, and technical decisions across both the desktop and backend sides of the product, while also owning strategy, budget, and the growth of your staff. The right candidate brings strong experience running agile teams, experience managing managers or team leads, deep expertise in system architecture, and a track record of leading distributed, remote-first engineering teams. You bring 7+ years of engineering management experience and enthusiasm for how AI-assisted development is changing the way software gets built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the full Computer Backup engineering team, which reports into this role, with Desktop and Backend Leads running the day-to-day of their areas.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the long-term technical direction for Computer Backup, ensuring architecture and platform decisions hold up as the product and customer base grow.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the multi-quarter delivery strategy for Computer Backup, and partner with Product leadership to help set the roadmap and negotiate scope, schedule, and priorities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold accountability for the team’s budget and spend, aligning headcount, tooling, and infrastructure investment with business priorities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make technical and organizational decisions with broad, long-term impact, including shared platform components and infrastructure that other teams depend on.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the desktop and backend areas operate well together, with shared goals and a consistent agile delivery process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide oversight of the team’s agile process, ensuring ceremonies such as sprint planning, backlog refinement, standups, and retrospectives are run well and consistently across both areas.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own delivery across the client and backend, from planning and design through implementation and post-launch support, partnering with dedicated QA and release teams for testing and delivery.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the reliability, performance, and maintainability of the backup client and backend services that customers depend on to protect their data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion engineering quality by growing unit testing and other automated test coverage, and by keeping testing a first-class part of how the team builds and ships software.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part hands-on in code reviews, architecture decisions, and technical problem-solving across both desktop and server work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion the effective use of AI-assisted development tools, guide the team in adopting agentic coding practices, and help establish norms around AI-augmented workflows.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve team productivity by identifying bottlenecks, refining processes, and investing in tooling and practices that help engineers do their best work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate directly with senior leadership and major customers on significant matters, represent the team in executive reviews, and communicate risks and trade-offs with clear recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of engineering management experience, including managing managers or team leads, ideally in a cloud, SaaS, desktop software, or platform engineering environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting long-term technical direction and system architecture for a growing product or platform.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning multi-quarter technical and delivery strategy and helping shape a product roadmap.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience negotiating scope, schedule, and priorities with product and senior leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accountability for a team or departmental budget, including resourcing and investment decisions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with agile development processes, including scrum, sprint planning, backlog management, estimation, and retrospectives, with a track record of ensuring these ceremonies are run well and consistently for a delivery team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing distributed, remote engineering teams, including strong async communication and remote collaboration practices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software engineering background with deep expertise in system architecture, able to engage hands-on in technical discussions, design reviews, and architectural decisions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid command of the full software development lifecycle, from requirements and design through deployment and production support.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong commitment to engineering quality, including the value of unit testing and automated test coverage, and a track record of building testing into a team’s everyday practice.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering software across desktop clients, backend services, or both.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communicator and negotiator, able to work directly with senior leadership and major customers and to escalate risks early with clear recommendations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI agentic coding tools such as Claude Code and Codex is a plus; we actively use them and value leaders who encourage their adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Backblaze&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the organization building software that protects the data of hundreds of thousands of customers worldwide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a complete product end to end, from the desktop experience customers see to the backend that keeps their data safe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the strategy, structure, and leadership team of a core product line, with direct access to senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with experienced engineering, product, and QA teams in a flat, low-bureaucracy environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation and benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote-first culture supporting work-life balance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To provide greater transparency to candidates, we share base pay ranges for all US-based job postings regardless of state. We set standard base pay ranges for all roles based on function, level, and country location, benchmarked against similar-stage growth companies. Final offer amounts are determined by multiple factors, including candidate location, skills, depth of work experience, and relevant licenses/credentials, and may vary from the amounts listed below.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected salary range for this role is $205,000-$255,000.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At this point, we hope you&#39;re feeling excited about the job description you&#39;re reading. Even if you don&#39;t meet every requirement, we still encourage you to apply. Learning, developing, and growing are key parts of our culture. We&#39;re eager to meet people who believe in our mission and can contribute to our team in various ways. We want people to feel comfortable expressing their true selves and to come, stay, and do their best work here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Backblaze, we value being fair and good to our customers, partners, and employees. That&#39;s why diversity, equity, and inclusion are at the core of our values. We are committed to fostering a workforce where all employees feel a sense of belonging regardless of race, ethnicity, nationality, gender, sexual orientation, age, religion, socio-economic status, ability, veteran status, and education. We believe that our dedication to cultivating a diverse workspace not only allows us to better serve our customers in over 175 countries but further reinforces our commitment to doing the right thing. We are proud to be an &lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;About Backblaze&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backblaze is the object storage leader in the open cloud movement, fueling customer success with cloud storage built purposefully to unlock budgets, unburden administrators, and unleash innovators. Together with our partners, we’re helping customers break free from the restrictive, overpriced legacy solutions that hold them back, and blaze forward with the full power of the open cloud in their hands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Manager, Site Reliability Engineer &lt;/strong&gt;to join our team and help ensure the stability, scalability, and reliability of Backblaze production systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced Senior Manager to lead within our Site Reliability Engineering (SRE) organization. The ideal candidate brings deep experience developing engineering strategies, leading high-performing technical teams, and translating reliability priorities into measurable outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a leader at Backblaze, you will work across the organization to help achieve our reliability and operational goals, including partnering with engineering leaders, executives, customers, and other key stakeholders. This role will focus on unlocking the potential of our engineers through observability, automation, operational excellence, and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hire, lead, mentor, and develop a high-performing team of Site Reliability Engineers, including coaching, career development, and performance management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage other engineering managers as required and help develop leadership capability within the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Establish team goals, objectives, and reliability priorities, ensuring commitments are delivered or expectations are proactively reset when circumstances change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with engineering leaders across Backblaze to define strategic priorities and execution plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop and improve automation that accelerates the deployment of new storage vaults, core servers, and supporting infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own and improve vulnerability management and patching schedules to ensure contractual, operational, and security requirements are met.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive complex reliability initiatives from problem discovery through implementation and resolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with engineering teams to improve observability, monitoring, and alerting and provide meaningful insight into the health and performance of Backblaze infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead analysis of SLA and reliability performance, identify areas of risk, and drive corrective actions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Participate in leadership on-call rotations, major incident response, and post-incident reviews to continuously improve service reliability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide leadership during incidents and ensure root cause analyses, corrective actions, and follow-up work are completed effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply established ITIL and operational processes across incident, change, problem, and capacity management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with Engineering, Customer Success, Product, and Operations teams to support resilient system design and reliable production operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engage with customers to understand their reliability needs and ensure stability priorities reflect customer experiences and business requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work with vendors and service providers to troubleshoot service issues and monitor SLA performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead cross-functional initiatives to identify gaps in observability, operational processes, reliability, and infrastructure management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify recurring operational issues and develop long-term strategies and action plans to address them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Document systems, share learnings, and promote a reliability-focused engineering culture across Backblaze.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Right Fit&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;10+ years of experience in site reliability engineering, systems engineering, infrastructure, or production operations, including significant engineering leadership experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated experience building, managing, mentoring, and developing high-performing technical teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience leading reliability or infrastructure organizations operating large-scale, production-grade systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong understanding of deploying and managing large fleets of Linux hosts, with a strong emphasis on automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong knowledge of observability and monitoring technologies such as VictoriaMetrics, Prometheus, Grafana, OpenSearch, or comparable platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience establishing operational procedures, runbooks, incident processes, and reliability practices at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong understanding of storage systems, including storage performance, sharding, distributed architectures, and storage algorithms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Understanding of load-balancing technologies and services, including IPVS or comparable technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience managing security-focused infrastructure operations, including patching, hardening, vulnerability identification, and remediation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead major incidents and post-incident processes, including root cause analysis and corrective action planning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience using automation and AI-assisted technologies to improve engineering productivity, system performance, operational efficiency, or scalability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to independently take ownership of complex problems and drive initiatives from discovery through resolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong communication and collaboration skills, with the ability to work effectively with engineers, executives, customers, vendors, and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus Points For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience operating infrastructure at hyperscale or within a hyperscaler environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience in SaaS, cloud infrastructure, service provider, storage, or large-scale distributed systems environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with object storage or other large-scale storage platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with ITIL or OSS operational practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience defining, managing, and improving SLOs and SLAs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with AWS, Google Cloud Platform, Microsoft Azure, or other major cloud platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience leading teams through significant infrastructure scaling, reliability, or operational transformation initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Backblaze Perks&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
