&lt;p&gt;To provide greater transparency to candidates, Backblaze shares base pay ranges for U.S.-based positions. Compensation ranges are established based on factors including function, level, and location. Final offers may vary based on candidate location, relevant experience, skills, and applicable licenses or credentials.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected salary range for this role is $178,000 - $210,000.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Backblaze, we value being fair and good to our customers, partners, and employees. That’s why diversity, equity, and inclusion are at the core of our values. We are committed to fostering a workforce where all employees feel a sense of belonging regardless of race, ethnicity, nationality, gender, sexual orientation, age, religion, socio-economic status, ability, veteran status, and education. We believe that our dedication to cultivating a diverse workspace not only allows us to better serve our customers in over 175 countries, but further reinforces our commitment to doing the right thing. We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To understand more about the data we collect and process as part of your application, please view our &lt;a href=&quot;https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63d32de856f6323a43a277f2/64b0660cd90ac9b4953f7f1d_Backblaze_HR_Employee_Related_Privacy_Notice.pdf&quot;&gt;Backblaze Employee Privacy Notice.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior individual contributor role with significant architectural ownership. You will set the technical direction for how Backblaze detects, correlates, and responds to infrastructure incidents across our data centers, and you will mentor other engineers on the team as that platform matures. If you have a passion for making complex distributed systems visible, you are comfortable making architecture decisions that will outlive your tenure, and you are excited about applying AI and agentic automation to infrastructure operations, this role was built for you..&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical direction and standards for observability across the organization, including instrumentation conventions, alerting philosophy, and dashboard design patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers on the Observability team and act as a technical resource for SRE, Storage Engineering, and Network Engineering on observability practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead design reviews for observability work and represent the team in cross-functional architecture discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate build-versus-buy decisions for observability and AIOps tooling, including data sovereignty and compliance considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce and maintain design documentation, runbooks, and architectural decision records that make the platform operable and extensible by future contributors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Observability Platform&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve our metrics pipeline, including VictoriaMetrics, Prometheus, and the Consul-based service discovery layer that keeps scrape targets current as infrastructure scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and expand our logging stack (OpenSearch, Logstash, and Filebeat) across all Backblaze data centers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and expand distributed tracing with Jaeger and OpenTelemetry, extending coverage beyond the current application instrumentation to new services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and maintain Grafana dashboard standards for infrastructure, storage, and application performance visibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive expansion of internal application telemetry in partnership with application teams to improve visibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define capacity and retention strategy for the telemetry stack as the fleet grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure &amp;amp; Automation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own infrastructure-as-code for observability stack deployments across multiple Kubernetes clusters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and review automated playbooks for configuration management and automation across Debian-based bare metal servers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the SRE team on Consul-based service discovery for VictoriaMetrics scrape target automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Ceph storage observability, including OSD health, performance metrics, and integration with alerting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Network Engineering team on BGP, routing, and network-level observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in a systems engineering, SRE, DevOps, or observability-focused role, including demonstrated technical leadership on a platform or infrastructure team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on experience with Prometheus, VictoriaMetrics, or equivalent metrics platforms, including PromQL, Alertmanager, and operating these systems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and operating log aggregation pipelines such as Elasticsearch/OpenSearch, Logstash, Filebeat, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of distributed tracing (Jaeger, OpenTelemetry, or equivalent), including instrumentation strategy, not just operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and/or Go for automation and tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Kubernetes, including deploying workloads and understanding pod networking and storage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with infrastructure-as-code tooling and configuration management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of Linux internals, with Debian/Ubuntu preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience mentoring engineers and raising the technical bar on a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills. You&#39;ll work across engineering, SRE, security, and leadership, and you&#39;ll be expected to write design documents that drive decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading the evaluation or deployment of AIOps tooling, including alert correlation, deduplication, or automated root cause analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building, deploying, or operating AI agents or agentic AI systems. This is a strong differentiator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with LLM APIs (Anthropic, OpenAI) or self-hosted LLM inference in an infrastructure context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Ceph storage, including OSD management, pool configuration, and CRUSH maps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with incident management platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with BGP, network observability, or working in multi-DC environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with secrets management in production environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in a regulated or compliance-driven environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a storage-focused company or hyperscale infrastructure environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Work On&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A telemetry stack spanning several data centers with exabytes of storage under observation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real infrastructure at scale: Kubernetes, Ceph, Vitess, KVM, and a custom storage platform serving hundreds of thousands of customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative team that values engineering excellence, transparency, and operational rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To provide greater transparency to candidates, we share base pay ranges for all US-based job postings regardless of state. Final offer amounts are determined by multiple factors including candidate location, skills, depth of work experience, and relevant licenses/credentials.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The expected salary range for this role is $178,000 - $200,000 plus 10% target annual bonus and RSUs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Backblaze, we value being fair and good to our customers, partners, and employees. Diversity, equity, and inclusion are at the core of our values. We are committed to fostering a workforce where all employees feel a sense of belonging regardless of race, ethnicity, nationality, gender, sexual orientation, age, religion, socio-economic status, ability, veteran status, and education. We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Sr. Partner Marketing Manager&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Remote – US&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Backblaze&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backblaze (NASDAQ: BLZE) is the high-performance capacity storage layer for AI. Founded in 2007, we scaled the business on less than $3 million in outside funding until our 2021 IPO on the Nasdaq. Today we manage over five billion gigabytes of data for 500K+ customers in 175+ countries, including AI platforms, GPU clouds, businesses, developers, IT professionals, and individuals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a best of breed storage platform, a robust partner ecosystem is how Backblaze reaches the AI market: GPU clouds, AI infrastructure vendors, data and AI platforms, and the events where that ecosystem gathers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will serve our Partnerships &amp;amp; Ecosystem team, and report to the VP of Marketing. Product Marketing, Campaign leads, Content and Creative, Demand Generation, Communications, and Analyst Relations all back you up as you provide the bridge between corporate GTM efforts and our partner orgs GTM efforts. You work at a senior level and carry the work yourself, with strong collaboration and teams to support your efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The job is to give partner marketing the same structure, standards, and ambition as everything else Marketing does, and to make every partnership worth more to Backblaze, to the partner, and to the customers we share.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set the plan and the operating rhythm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run a rolling six-month partner marketing plan with the Partner team with a focus on priority partnerships in the AI space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structure the work in manner that keeps the teams aligned and informed with shared calendars, clear intake paths, and a point of view on what Backblaze will and won’t do&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fold partner marketing into Marketing’s broader planning so partner programs, launches, and campaigns move with brand, product marketing, and demand generation priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay agile and responsive as opportunities evolve and shift around you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the reporting cadence on impact, in collaboration with the business intelligence team, at a level consumable from c-suite to team meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate our story for partners&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take Product Marketing’s core positioning and materials and adapt them for each partner’s sellers, architects, and customers: joint value propositions, partner-facing narratives, and co-branded messaging that stay true to how Backblaze talks about itself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equip priority partners’ teams to get Backblaze right, with kits, one-pagers, and sales plays built alongside Enablement and Partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build brand with the ecosystem&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise Backblaze’s profile with the most credible names in AI through joint narratives, co-presented content, webinars, and thought leadership that establish Backblaze as a storage leader for AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate announcements with Communications, including the disclosure requirements that come with being a public company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with the events team, advocate for Backblaze’s presence at AI-first events and moments where we can show up with strategic partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bridge marketing and enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with the content and creative team, build co-branded reference architectures, joint case studies and customer references, and informative announcements that help customers make decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with DevRel and Sales Engineering around content and enablement with technical depth, they can provide the substance but you’ll need to provide structure and promotion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own how Backblaze appears on partner surfaces: integration and partner pages, directories, marketplace listings, co-branded assets, and Powered By Backblaze materials, and documentation. Keep them accurate, current, and consistent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support analyst submissions for partner-validated architectures alongside our Analyst Relations team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The Right Fit&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7–10 years in B2B technology marketing, including 4+ years in partner, alliance, or ecosystem marketing at an infrastructure, cloud, data, or AI company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of launching and running co-marketing with partners larger than your own company, and of earning priority from a partner’s marketing team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven skill at translating core product positioning into partner-specific narratives, and the writing ability to draft them yourself. Bring samples&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency to work with Sales Engineers and partner architects: cloud and object storage, S3-compatible APIs, and how AI and data pipelines use storage (training data, checkpoints, inference)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience planning and executing a presence at major industry conferences, ideally in the AI ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort reading pipeline and campaign data in Salesforce and dashboards that others build, and turning it into decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The discipline to work solo: set priorities, hold them, and use AI tools to multiply your output without lowering the bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strongly Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner marketing experience at an AI cloud, AI infrastructure vendor, or data platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with partner-hosted conferences and co-presented programming at GTC scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public company experience, including work within disclosure requirements for partner announcements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience standing up partner marketing in a function that did not have a home.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background producing technical proof: reference architectures, benchmark-backed content, and customer references.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Logistics&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Remote – US&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; ~25%, concentrated around major AI events and partner meetings&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/strong&gt; VP, Marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partners with:&lt;/strong&gt; Partnerships &amp;amp; Ecosystem, Product Marketing, Revenue Operations, Channel Marketing, Content and Creative, Demand Generation, Communications, Analyst Relations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Backblaze Perks&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare for family, including dental and vision&lt;/li&gt;
