&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;yco28j&quot; data-start=&quot;83&quot; data-end=&quot;101&quot;&gt;About Backblaze&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;103&quot; data-end=&quot;506&quot;&gt;Backblaze is the object storage leader in the open cloud movement, fueling customer success with cloud storage built purposefully to unlock budgets, unburden administrators, and unleash innovators. Together with our partners, we’re helping customers break free from the restrictive, overpriced legacy solutions that hold them back, and blaze forward with the full power of the open cloud in their hands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;508&quot; data-end=&quot;921&quot;&gt;Founded in 2007, we scaled the business with less than $3 million in outside funding until 2021, when we did a traditional IPO on the Nasdaq stock exchange. Today, Backblaze generates over $100m in revenue and is the leading specialized storage cloud, managing over three billion gigabytes of data storage for 500K+ customers in 175+ countries, including businesses, developers, IT professionals, and individuals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;923&quot; data-end=&quot;1085&quot;&gt;But while there is a lot to celebrate in our past, there is almost as much opportunity ahead of us. We’re seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Staff Product Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to join our team!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backblaze’s B2 cloud object storage offers multi-exabyte, S3-compatible, globally available object storage that unlocks app builder innovation across AI neoclouds and traditional hyperscalers at a fraction of the cost from traditional cloud infrastructure hyperscalers. The Staff Product Manager for B2 will work closely with key stakeholders to understand the evolution of cloud storage and the customer problems in the space and determine product strategies and roadmap to address those problems. He or she will work independently to lead the efforts for new feature discovery and delivery and improvements to execute on those strategies. Understanding customer problems through interviews and market research and translating them into requirements is critical.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive B2 product strategy and roadmap development through to delivery execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the end-to-end product development lifecycle from discovery through delivery in feature development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather and synthesize inputs for discovery and prioritization from internal functions, customers, and partners across the full spectrum of R&amp;amp;D development of feature capabilities, user experience challenges, cost optimization, and technical debt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex customer challenges into clear, concise and actionable product requirements in collaboration with Design, Engineering and GTM teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product Marketing to launch and drive adoption of new products and features. Act as a subject matter expert and evangelist for Backblazes solutions solutions, presenting to customers, prospects, partners, and to internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and track key product metrics (KPIs), using data to guide iteration and growth decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a deep understanding of the latest advancements in the object storage market across its application in customer use cases and competitive offerings to identify new opportunities and ensure Backblaze’s market leadership position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Right Fit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of Product Management experience in tech businesses, preferably on IaaS and/or SaaS offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of successfully launching and scaling technical products / platforms in high-growth businesses involving in-depth cross-functional collaboration and leadership across R&amp;amp;D and go-to-market functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong grasp of cloud architecture, APIs, and security and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success in owning product roadmaps, defining MVPs, and driving the complete product life cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinker who can translate market trends, customer needs, and technical innovations into a clear product vision and actionable roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep empathy for customers / users in gathering and synthesizing input and a passion for solving their most pressing security challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication and leadership skills with a collaborative and team-oriented approach to identifying problems, determining potential solutions, and building consensus around your vision with internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying data and metrics to inform product decisions and measure success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Point For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in cloud storage and computing from hyperscale and neocloud providers, such as AWS, Azure, GCP, GPU clouds, CDNs, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Application development programming experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in applying GenAI in solution prototyping and agentic workflow development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
